Problem Statement: Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a target value, return the index if the target is found. If not, return the index where it would be if it were inserted in order.
You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.

Example 1:
Input: nums = [1,3,5,6], target = 5
Output: 2

Example 2:
Input: nums = [1,3,5,6], target = 2
Output: 1

Example 3:
Input: nums = [1,3,5,6], target = 7
Output: 4

Source Code:
class Solution {
    public int searchInsert(int[] nums, int target) {
        int l = 0;
        int h = nums.length-1;
        int mid=0;
        while (l <= h){
            mid = (l+h)/2;
            if (nums[mid]==target){
                return mid;
            }
            else if(nums[mid]>target){
                h=mid-1;
            }
            else {
                l = mid+1;
            }
        }
        return l;
        
    }
}

Issues Faced: Finding which among the variables of the binary search correctly relates to the position of the target index to be inserted.  
